    },
    "message": "Make the demo-v2 simulation screen easier to read and operate\n\n- Move the compute controls into their own enlarged panel between the map and the event timeline\n- Rename the play buttons to \"シミュレーションを再生\" so playback is not mistaken for computing\n- Group timeline events under a heading, color them by outcome (blue resolved, red unresolved, gray progress), wrap them in a grid instead of a horizontal scroller, and give every event type a plain Japanese name\n- Point the issues panel at the event timeline and explain unresolved support requests concretely\n- Tell users to finish or stop computing before intervening\n- Put the branch comparison target next to the layer selector and enlarge it\n- Use the branch icon for intervention headings\n- Mark the report as a draft until the run is computed to the end\n- Enlarge the evacuee/staff status panel and open a status popup when a person is selected\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
